# Run Gradle from the correct build directory

This repo is **two independent Gradle builds** with their own wrappers pinned to
different Gradle versions (ADR-0015). Running `./gradlew` from the wrong directory
silently uses the wrong toolchain and fails or misbehaves.

| Build | Run from | Wrapper | Modules |
|-------|----------|---------|---------|
| SDK build | repo root | Gradle 8.11.1 (`./gradlew`) | `protocol`, `sdk-android`, samples, plugin |
| studio build | `studio/` | Gradle 9.3.1 (`studio/gradlew`) | `engine`, `shared`, `desktopApp` |

## Rules

- **Chain an absolute `cd` inside the command; do NOT rely on the Shell `working_directory`
  parameter alone** — in this environment it is not reliably applied, so `./gradlew` silently
  runs from the repo root (8.11.1) even when `working_directory` says `studio`. Always write
  `cd /abs/path/to/repo/studio && ./gradlew …`.
- To build/test/run **`engine`, `shared`, or `desktopApp`**, run studio's wrapper. NEVER run
  these from the repo root — root's `./gradlew` is 8.11.1 and does not know these modules.
- `protocol` is the seam: `:protocol:publishToMavenLocal` is a **root** task and must be run
  (from repo root) before the studio build, which consumes `wailo-protocol` from Maven Local.

```bash
# studio (engine/shared/desktopApp) — absolute cd, then studio's ./gradlew (9.3.1)
cd /abs/path/to/repo/studio && ./gradlew :shared:jvmTest
cd /abs/path/to/repo/studio && ./gradlew :desktopApp:run

# SDK build (protocol/sdk-android/samples/plugin) — from repo root (8.11.1)
cd /abs/path/to/repo && ./gradlew :protocol:publishToMavenLocal
cd /abs/path/to/repo && ./gradlew :sample-android:assembleDebug
```

## Studio dev loop: check `hotRun` before you compile

The studio desktop app is usually already running under **Compose Hot Reload auto mode**
(`cd studio && ./gradlew :desktopApp:hotRun --auto`) in one of the user's terminals. Auto mode
**continuously recompiles and hot-reloads on every source edit**, so a manual studio build is
redundant and slow — and a second sandboxed `./gradlew` can even fail on stale caches.

**Before running any studio compile/build/run, check whether `hotRun` is already live:**

- Look in the terminals folder for a terminal whose `active_command` contains
  `:desktopApp:hotRun` (its output shows `Compose Hot Reload` and `> :desktopApp:hotRun` / `> IDLE`).
- **If it IS running:** do NOT run `:desktopApp:run` or a manual `compileKotlin`/`build`. Just
  edit the source — hot reload rebuilds automatically. Read that terminal's file to confirm the
  reload and to surface any compile errors.
- **If it is NOT running:** build/run/compile normally (above), or start it with
  `cd studio && ./gradlew :desktopApp:hotRun --auto`.

`hotRun` only covers the running app — tests (e.g. `:shared:jvmTest`) are a separate task and
still need their own invocation.

Prefer the `rgradlew` skill's remote path only for the SDK/Android build; the studio
build needs `wailo-protocol` in local Maven, so build it locally from `studio/`.
